.gradle/
build/
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store
local.properties
*.patch
*.txt

# Signing material - the actual RELEASE keystore must never be committed. CI
# decodes it from the ARKSTER_RELEASE_KEYSTORE_BASE64 secret at build time
# instead; see .github/workflows/release.yml. If you keep a local copy for
# manual `assembleRelease` builds, it belongs outside the repo or ignored here.
# debug.keystore is the opposite case - its credentials are the public,
# well-known Android debug defaults (storePassword/keyPassword "android",
# alias "androiddebugkey"), not a secret, and it's meant to be committed and
# shared so every build of this app - yours, any other contributor's, CI -
# signs debug APKs identically. See app/build.gradle.kts's signingConfigs
# block. Same exception the sibling ARKarium reader's own .gitignore makes.
*.keystore
*.jks
!debug.keystore
*.keystore.b64
